  "id": "COMPOUND:23657 - PROTEIN:5003",
  "verbalization": "Eryvarin D is shown to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is involved in epigenetic regulation of gene expression. This complex is known to target histone methyltransferases, and its inhibition has been linked to the suppression of tumor growth and metastasis. The evidence suggests that Eryvarin D acts as a modulator of this complex, potentially through direct binding to its components. The pathway also includes Ponfolin, which is a known target of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, further reinforcing the role of this complex in the mechanism of action of Eryvarin D. The integration of these targets indicates that Eryvarin D may exert its effects by inhibiting the PRC2 complex, thereby altering the epigenetic landscape and influencing cellular processes associated with disease. The consistent evidence across the three paths supports a mechanistic link between Eryvarin D and ME-180, highlighting the importance of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex in this relationship.",
